BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery Plan) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 705.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 683.5 Td (Document Owner: Office of Business Resilience) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 669.5 Td (Classification: Internal - Restricted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 655.5 Td (Version: 4.2 | Effective Date: 2026-07-08) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 635.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 609.5 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 586.5 Td (This Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery \(BC/DR\) Plan establishes the strategy, roles, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 572.5 Td (procedures HPE uses to sustain and recover critical operations during a disruptive event. It covers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558.5 Td (HPE's customer-facing GreenLake hybrid cloud platform, the SAP S/4HANA enterprise resource planning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 544.5 Td (\(ERP\) environment, and the supporting infrastructure, data, and personnel required to keep essential) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 530.5 Td (functions running. The plan applies to all HPE production data centers, colocation facilities, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 516.5 Td (the teams responsible for their operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 496.5 Td (The objective is simple: minimize downtime, protect data, safeguard people, and honor commitments to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 482.5 Td (customers, partners, and regulators through disciplined preparation and rehearsed response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 462.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 436.5 Td (2. Business Impact Analysis \(BIA\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 413.5 Td (The foundation of this plan is HPE's Business Impact Analysis, refreshed at least annually and after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 399.5 Td (any material change to the technology estate. The BIA identifies critical processes and essential) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 385.5 Td (functions, ranks them by operational and financial impact, and establishes the tolerances that drive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371.5 Td (our recovery investments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 351.5 Td (| Critical Process | Tier | RTO | RPO |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 338.5 Td (| --- | --- | --- | --- |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 325.5 Td (| GreenLake control plane & customer workloads | 0 | 1 hour | 5 minutes |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 312.5 Td (| SAP S/4HANA ERP \(finance, order-to-cash, supply chain\) | 0 | 2 hours | 15 minutes |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 299.5 Td (| Identity, authentication & API gateways | 1 | 1 hour | 5 minutes |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 286.5 Td (| Customer support & entitlement systems | 1 | 4 hours | 30 minutes |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 273.5 Td (| Corporate collaboration & email | 2 | 8 hours | 4 hours |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 254.5 Td (Each recovery time objective \(RTO\) defines the maximum tolerable outage before impact becomes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 240.5 Td (unacceptable, while each recovery point objective \(RPO\) defines the maximum tolerable data loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 226.5 Td (measured backward from the moment of disruption. These recovery targets are the contract between the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 212.5 Td (business and the recovery teams; every technical control below exists to satisfy a documented point) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 198.5 Td (objective.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 178.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 152.5 Td (3. Data Protection: Backup, Replication, and Immutability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 129.5 Td (HPE protects data through layered strategy designed to meet the RPOs above:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 109.5 Td (- Immutable backups. All Tier 0 and Tier 1 datasets are written to write-once, immutable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 95.5 Td (  repositories with enforced retention locks. Because these copies cannot be altered or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 81.5 Td (  deleted-even with administrative credentials-they provide a clean recovery source that is) Tj ET
endstream
