6 0 obj
<< /Length 4063 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (  resilient to ransomware and insider threats.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (- Snapshots. Application-consistent snapshots of SAP S/4HANA \(HANA System Replication savepoints) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (  and log backups\) and GreenLake volumes are captured on short intervals to satisfy the 5-15) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (  minute RPO windows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682.0 Td (- Replication. Continuous asynchronous and, for the most critical databases, synchronous) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668.0 Td (  replication mirrors production data to a geographically separate recovery region, ensuring an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654.0 Td (  up-to-date copy is always available to restore from.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 640.0 Td (- Restore verification. Backups are meaningless if they cannot be recovered. Automated restore) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 626.0 Td (  rehearsals sample production data sets weekly and confirm integrity, recoverability, and elapsed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612.0 Td (  time against the RTO.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 592.0 Td (The 3-2-1-1 principle governs all Tier 0 data: three copies, on two media types, one off-site, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 578.0 Td (one immutable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 532.0 Td (4. Recovery Architecture: Failover and Alternate Sites) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 509.0 Td (HPE operates a multi-site topology engineered for redundancy and rapid failover:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 489.0 Td (- The primary region hosts live GreenLake and SAP S/4HANA production workloads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 475.0 Td (- A hot-site in a separate region maintains synchronously replicated data and warm-started) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 461.0 Td (  compute, enabling near-immediate automated failover for Tier 0 services within their RTO.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 447.0 Td (- A warm-site provides pre-provisioned but scaled-down capacity for Tier 1 and Tier 2 services,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 433.0 Td (  activated on demand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 419.0 Td (- A contracted alternate cloud region serves as an additional recovery landing zone if a primary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 405.0 Td (  provider or facility becomes wholly unavailable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 385.0 Td (Network redundancy, load-balanced ingress, and diverse carrier paths eliminate single points of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371.0 Td (failure. Failover procedures are codified as runbooks and, where possible, automated so that human) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 357.0 Td (error during a crisis is minimized.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 337.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 311.0 Td (5. Crisis Governance, Succession, and Communications) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 284.0 Td (Leadership and Succession) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 268.5 Td (A standing Crisis Management Team \(CMT\) directs response. To ensure decisions are never blocked by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 254.5 Td (an unavailable leader, every CMT role has a documented succession chain with named alternates,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 240.5 Td (deputies, and backup personnel. Authority delegation is pre-approved so that if a primary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 226.5 Td (decision-maker cannot be reached, the designated deputy assumes command without delay.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 202.5 Td (Crisis Communications) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 187.0 Td (The crisis communications protocol governs how and when we inform stakeholders. Upon activation, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 173.0 Td (CMT issues structured notification to employees, affected customers, partners, regulators, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 159.0 Td (executive leadership through primary and out-of-band channels. Pre-drafted holding statements, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 145.0 Td (incident bridge, and a status page keep GreenLake customers informed of service state and expected) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131.0 Td (recovery, while account teams manage direct outreach for enterprise SAP-dependent customers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 111.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 85.0 Td (6. Testing, Exercises, and Validation) Tj ET
endstream
